From 71a9dc7cff6fa88decc4bb4ae820a0f29165d512 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Catalin Niculescu <cn.cata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:05:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Noise limits, the noise spec, and sustained step-down
 measurements

- noise.py / NOISE.md: percent -> rpm (rpm ~ 300 + 25 x %, anchored on the
  display's 600 rpm at 12 %), rpm -> dB at the ears (the user's phone
  readings), warning bands, and the limits: 600 rpm in quiet hours
  (weekdays 22:00-07:00), 2000 rpm by day; all overridable in
  ~/.config/llano/noise.json.
- llano.py caps every speed to the limit in force (logged with the speed
  asked for); `loud` lifts it until quiet hours end (2 h by day), `quiet`
  restores it; `enforce` lowers a software-set speed above it and leaves
  the roller alone; `noise` prints the limit. Status output adds a
  `noise {json}` line.
- contrib/llano-enforce.{service,timer} + install-enforcer.sh: a user
  timer running `llano.py enforce` every 5 minutes and at 22:00.
- research/step_down.py: 100 -> 0 % in 10 % steps, CPU (whole threads),
  GPU (CUDA duty cycle) or both, 45 s per step, pad untouched (600 rpm);
  results for CPU then GPU, and both together. lut_sweep's idle check
  takes the median of three GPU readings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
